4B7B Absorption spectroscopy operating procedures
Deflate:
1. Perform the "light off" operation;
2. Turn off the 6517B reading. Press the "LOCAL" and "Z-CHK" keys of the 6517B galvanometer to display "ZeroCheck"
3. Turn off the power of the molecular pump and wait for its speed to return to zero (it may take a long time);
4. Turn off the power supply of the dry pump solenoid valve (you can also turn off the power supply of the dry pump);
5. Loosen the knob of the injection window of the sample chamber and ensure that the pressure in the sample chamber exceeds one atmosphere before the injection window can be opened;
6. Open the nitrogen valve, open the bleed valve on the dry pump, and fill the sample chamber with nitrogen;
7. After the injection window leaks, close the nitrogen valve and the bleed valve on the dry pump; note that during a period of time around July when there is high temperature and humidity, it is recommended to vent nitrogen to prevent moisture from entering the sample chamber, which can significantly reduce the vacuuming time;
Replace the device to be calibrated:
1. Open the hinged door with a window (that is, the injection window of the sample chamber);
2. Replace the sample. Note: Please be sure to wear gloves (disposable or nitrile) for operation; it is strictly forbidden to touch components and samples in the vacuum with bare hands;
3. Close the nitrogen valve and the bleed valve on the dry pump;
4. Close the trapdoor with window.
Vacuuming:
1. Confirm that the bleed valve is closed;
2. Turn on the power of the dry pump and solenoid valve, and start rough vacuuming of the sample chamber;
3. After 2 minutes when the sound of the dry pump decreases significantly, turn on the power of the molecular pump;
4. After the molecular pump speed reaches the rated speed, turn on the vacuum gauge. The indication should be better than a certain empirical value such as 3E-4Pa, so as to make a preliminary judgment that there is no air leakage;
5. When the vacuum degree of the sample chamber reaches a good level of 1e-6Pa, spectroscopy experiments can be carried out;
6. After performing the "turn on" operation, start the experiment.
